dows sweep since: tests/unit/metrics/test_git_metrics.py::test_oracle_cap_change_events_compares_unsampled_adjacent_revisions and ::test_history_walk_cat_file_starts_do_not_grow_with_revisions, both at `git fast-import --quiet --export-marks=...` returned non-zero exit status 128 (helper `_fast_import_history`, tests/unit/metrics/test_git_metrics.py:220-250). Seen in tmp-branch runs 44900392763 and 44900397644 (2026-11-21 PST, trees on origin/main 1a11014a3a4). They block a green main `sweep (windows)`, which breezy-hogged-mastiff needs to close.\n\n## Hypothesis (unverified)\nThe helper passes the stream as text (`input=\"...\"` with text mode), so on Windows each \\\\n is written to git's stdin as \\\\r\\\\n, while each `data <n>` count is the byte length with \\\\n only. fast-import then reads past or short of each data block and aborts. Check: rerun with stderr captured, or feed `input=...encode('utf-8')` without text mode, on a Windows run.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Both tests pass in a `sweep (windows)` run (run id recorded in a comment) with the cause recorded on this ticket.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"1a73-6936-59d9-4f49","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows sweep: test_git_metrics fast-import history helper fails with exit 128","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["6e5594f4-5729-4194-8436-0c01a184c93c","358a7342-4e7c-4986-91e1-481bcb142762"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795267732477818002,"uuid":"af8fdfcf-807f-48fc-baf3-45261c81f37f"}